     "t": "alert",
     "type": "TIP",
     "title": null,
     "text": "**GATE Exam Insight:** When multiplying any signal by a piecewise constant waveform (pulse train taking values $\\{+1, -1, 0\\}$), treat the operation as:\n- Amplitude Gating / Windowing where value is $0$.\n- Direct Transmission where value is $+1$.\n- Phase Inversion ($180^\\circ$ phase shift) where value is $-1$."
