     "t": "p",
     "text": "**Faculty Bridge to Subsequent Topics:**\nComputing the area under a signal is fundamentally equivalent to:\n1. Evaluating the Fourier Transform at zero frequency: $X(0) = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x(t)\\,dt$.\n2. Evaluating the Laplace Transform at $s = 0$: $X(s)|_{s=0} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x(t)\\,dt$.\n3. Generating higher-order singularity functions: integrating a step gives a ramp; integrating a ramp gives a parabola $p(t) = \\frac{1}{2}t^2 u(t)$."
