     "type": "WARNING",
     "title": null,
     "text": "**The Inverted Limit Sign Trap:** Students often forget that $\\int_b^a = -\\int_a^b$. When the lower limit is $+\\infty$, integrating backward across an impulse yields $-1$, not $+1$. Because the non-zero region is $t < -2$, the resulting step is left-sided: $-u(-t - 2)$!"
