     "t": "alert",
     "type": "WARNING",
     "title": null,
     "text": "**The Rectification Trap:** Taking the modulus of a sinusoid **ONLY** halves the fundamental period if the original signal oscillates symmetrically about zero ($DC = 0$). When a non-zero DC offset is present and the signal crosses zero, adjacent rectified lobes have different peak heights and shapes. Therefore, the period **DOES NOT HALVE** ($T_0 = T_0'$)."
